Just recently came back to Nethack after something like 10 years,
played a lot in college, ascended once back in the day.

Started up a new wizard, found a /oWishing on DL2, wished myself a +2
SDSM.  Found a blessed scroll of charging shortly after, still have the
scroll and the wand, so three wishes yet to be used.  Amulet of ESP a
couple levels later, which has helped keep me out of major trouble.

Moved through the Mines pretty quickly, got all the gems down at the
bottom, have donated to the priest in Minetown for protection as much
as cash allowed (and have lots more gems yet if I can find enough
shopkeepers to sell them to).  AC currently at -15 without ever having
found a single scroll of enchant armor.  Some minor hiccups from
moments of stupidity (picked up a grey stone at Mine's End without
checking it -- it was a loadstone rather than the guaranteed luckstone;
read an unidentified scroll at one point when I was short on identify
scrolls that turned out to be destroy armor and lost my CoMR, but was
able to replace it from a bones pile), but in general my first
seemingly really promising game since I started up again.  I think I
have most of the basics covered -- magic resistance/cancellation from
the cloak, reflection from SDSM, blessed unicorn horn for most minor
maladies, lots of various resistances from corpses.

One thing I don't have, however, is spellbooks.  An unfortunate (and
surprisingly early) encounter with a pyrolisk managed to take out every
one of the spellbooks I had at hand (I didn't find a single bag in the
dungeon before I finished Sokoban).  I found one blank spellbook, which
I made into identify, but since then, I've passed the 20,000 turn mark
on all my other memorized spells, so I have nothing (but identify) to
cast.

I've kept descending for now, as my gear has been allowing me to do a
good imitation of a barbarian, just pounding my way through the hordes
with hardly a scratch.  But I haven't seen a spellbook since I left the
Mines (now on the level with my quest portal), and I'm not too sanguine
about the idea of going much further down without more robust magical
defenses -- sooner or later, I'll be running into stuff I just don't
want to get close enough to melee, and I've been running through my
stash of wands in a hurry.

If I had even just a couple of spellbooks for spells I didn't want, I
could polypile them or erase and write new ones (have a blessed magic
marker too).  The RNG has been scarily good to me on every other count.
 What do you do when it just won't give you any spellbooks?  Do I just
descend a little further in the main branch and hope?  I certainly
don't want to be going up against my quest nemesis in this state.

(Another issue: does your probability of finding secret doors abruptly
go down at about DL10?  I've been having a heck of a time (s)earching
for doors even in places where I know they are on the last few levels,
taking hundreds of turns (or more) sometimes when it used to be that
I'd find most doors in 10-20 turns max.  Haven't seen any wands of
secret door detection, either, not that I ever thought I'd need them --
I usually sell them for early cash...)

Any advice much appreciated.



